WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:03.191
Your menu. On every screen. Always right.

00:05.417 --> 00:09.482
Printed menus go out of date. Prices
change. Dishes sell out.

00:09.482 --> 00:12.131
And someone has to fix every screen.

00:12.133 --> 00:15.851
Menu Board works the other way round. Menu
in, screens out.

00:15.851 --> 00:18.665
Import your menu, or start from an
example.

00:19.617 --> 00:22.366
Tell us how many TVs you have, and pick a
look.

00:22.366 --> 00:26.242
Autopilot lays out every screen, sized to
read from the queue.

00:26.242 --> 00:29.328
All thirty-eight dishes, across three TVs.

00:31.250 --> 00:34.322
When a dish sells out, your staff tap it
on their phone.

00:36.900 --> 00:39.666
Seconds later, it's struck through on the
TV.

00:42.383 --> 00:46.029
Want full control? Start from a blank
canvas in the studio.

00:46.033 --> 00:50.299
Add your menu, a deal that shows its
saving at today's prices,

00:50.299 --> 00:52.819
an Iftar countdown and a QR code.

00:54.233 --> 00:56.079
Publish, and it's on the screen.

00:56.983 --> 01:00.084
Made for Pakistan. Dish names in Urdu.

01:00.300 --> 01:03.021
Sehri and Iftar countdowns for your city.

01:03.417 --> 01:07.146
And emergency messages on every screen, in
Urdu too.

01:08.817 --> 01:11.153
See every TV, and what it's showing.

01:12.367 --> 01:14.424
Reports tell you what really played.

01:15.300 --> 01:19.253
And the Android TV app pairs with a code,
and starts on boot.

01:19.833 --> 01:22.615
Menu Board. Menu in. Screens out.

01:23.133 --> 01:24.259
Book a demo.
